# Generated-artifact watch list (ADR-037). One CLI glob per line
# (the truth glob grammar: `*`/`?` stop at `/`, `**` spans -- these are
# NEVER git pathspecs, and a line starting ':', '-' or '!' is refused).
#
# A claim watching a path matched here is REFUSED at intake: a watch on
# a generated file restales on every regeneration -- watch the SOURCE
# the generator reads instead, or file with
#   --generated-ok "<why the artifact itself is the fact>"
# (stored, counted, and decaying per ADR-032 so the judgment is
# re-asked).
#
# The template ships this list EMPTY: which artifacts are generated is
# a per-repository fact the template cannot know. A committed empty
# list means "nothing here is generated" -- conscious policy, silent.
# Deleting the file instead leaves the check dark (one advisory line
# per path filing says so). This file is CONSUMER-OWNED: `copier
# update` never overwrites it (_skip_if_exists).
#
# Examples:
#   dist/**
#   docs/api/generated/**
#   exercises/*/generated/**
